>
>Personally I don't have a fixed name for pets because in ghost levels you
>tend to get confuse which is your pet and which the wild one. 

Exactly! My pet gets a different name every time, and I usually
make up a nonsense name that starts with the same first letter
as my character class. As an elf I have had pets called Entropy,
Elephant, Eventually, and so on. When I meet a pet like this I
say "aha! there is an elf ghost here." A good way to remind yourself
what's in the ghost pile and if it's worth going after, plus what
monster is responsible for there being a ghost here and how to deal
with it.

Plus sometimes you get a pet up to a high level with over a hundred
hit points. You want to spot that dog quick and tame it, even if
your new character can't determine hit points, you can remember...

